# Technical Report: Axle Shock Mount Redesign

*Working engineering document. Grows as the project progresses.*

---

## 1. Scope

Redesign of a folded weld-on rear axle shock mount bracket for 3.25"
axle housings (F-150 / Tacoma class). Baseline geometry reverse-engineered
from commercial aftermarket parts documented to fail via bending fatigue
at the saddle radius and hole tearing.

---

## 2. Nomenclature

| Symbol | Description | Unit |
|--------|-------------|------|
| $m$ | Vehicle mass | kg |
| $b$ | Corner weight bias (rear axle share) | – |
| $n$ | Jounce G-load | – |
| $g$ | Gravitational acceleration (9.81) | m/s² |
| $\theta$ | Shock mounting angle from horizontal | deg |
| $F_s$ | Axial shock force (per bracket) | N |
| $M$ | Bending moment at saddle | N·mm |
| $Z$ | Section modulus of bracket cross-section | mm³ |
| $\sigma_b$ | Bending stress at saddle | MPa |
| $\tau$ | Shear stress at bolt hole | MPa |
| $\sigma_a$ | Alternating stress amplitude | MPa |
| $\sigma_m$ | Mean stress | MPa |
| $S_e$ | Endurance limit (corrected) | MPa |
| $S_u$ | Ultimate tensile strength | MPa |
| $n_f$ | Fatigue safety factor | – |

