## 3. Governing Equations

### 3.1 Dynamic load at the shock eyelet

Static load carried by one bracket:

$$W_{static} = \frac{m \cdot b \cdot g}{2}$$

Dynamic load from jounce impact:

$$F_{dynamic} = W_{static} \cdot n$$

Resolved along the shock axis:

$$F_s = \frac{F_{dynamic}}{\sin\theta}$$

### 3.2 Bending moment at the saddle

$$M = F_s \cdot H_{hole}$$

### 3.3 Section modulus of the folded bracket

Modeled as two parallel flanges of thickness $t$, height $h$, separated
by inner span $d$, bending about the horizontal saddle axis:

$$I_{flange} = \frac{t \cdot h^3}{12}$$

$$A_{flange} = t \cdot h$$

$$I_{total} = 2 I_{flange} + 2 A_{flange} \left(\frac{d}{2}\right)^2$$

$$Z = \frac{I_{total}}{h/2}$$

### 3.4 Bending stress at the saddle

$$\sigma_b = \frac{M}{Z}$$

### 3.5 Shear / bearing stress at the bolt hole

Bolt in double shear through two flanges:

$$\tau = \frac{F_s}{2 \cdot D_{hole} \cdot t}$$

### 3.6 Fatigue — modified Goodman criterion

Alternating and mean stress:

$$\sigma_a = \frac{\sigma_{max} - \sigma_{min}}{2}, \quad
\sigma_m = \frac{\sigma_{max} + \sigma_{min}}{2}$$

Goodman safety factor for infinite life ($N > 10^6$):

$$\frac{1}{n_f} = \frac{\sigma_a}{S_e} + \frac{\sigma_m}{S_u}$$

Bracket passes infinite-life check when $n_f \geq 1.5$.

---

## 4. Optimization Framework

### 4.1 Objective

Minimize peak von Mises stress at the saddle radius and bolt hole rim,
subject to a mass ceiling comparable to the baseline (~0.26 kg).

### 4.2 Design variables

| Variable | Baseline | Redesign range | Effect |
|----------|----------|----------------|--------|
| $R_{bend}$ | 4.8 mm | 4.8 – 8.0 mm | ↓ stress concentration |
| $H_{margin}$ | 20.0 mm | 12 – 20 mm | ↓ mass, ↑ hole tearing risk |
| $W_{gusset}$ | 38.1 mm | 25 – 45 mm | ↑ stiffness, ↑ mass |
| $H_{gusset}$ | 45.0 mm | 35 – 60 mm | ↑ stiffness, ↑ mass |
| Doubler ring thickness | 0 mm | 0 – 3 mm | ↓ hole stress, ↑ mass |

### 4.3 Fixed parameters (vehicle interface — cannot change)

$R_{axle}$, $S_{span}$, $D_{hole}$, $H_{hole}$, $T_{wall}$

### 4.4 Constraints

- Yield: $\sigma_{max} \leq 0.67 \cdot S_y$ (design factor on yield)
- Fatigue: $n_f \geq 1.5$
- Manufacturing: $R_{bend} \geq T_{wall}$ (press-brake rule)
- Packaging: no interference with leaf spring, brake line, or shock body
- Weld access: minimum 6 mm clearance on all weld paths

### 4.5 Optimization method

Manual parametric sweep; one variable changed at a time, held against
the baseline FEA setup, peak stress recorded. Convergence declared when
marginal stress reduction per unit mass drops below 5%.

